{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review and reform parental responsibility law in England and Wales",
        "additional_details": "We believe parental responsibility needs a clearer, coherent framework centred on children's welfare. Reform should clarify duties and decision-making powers, improve parenting education and early support, strengthen accountability, hear children's views and protect safe family relationships. It should also provide supported, decision-specific capacity assessments and proportionate, reviewable measures, without treating incapacity as automatic loss of parental status and include a regular statutory review.",
        "background": "Undertake a comprehensive review of parental responsibility law in England and Wales and bring forward legislation to clarify parental duties, strengthen child protection, improve family support and agency coordination, and provide safeguards for decision-making where mental capacity is an issue.",
